package "main"

// lex.literal.float.range-carveout (Constraint): the spec says a `.` followed
// by a non-digit is the selector operator, so `1.foo` should be the tokens
// `1` `.` `foo` (a field selector on int 1) and be rejected with the selector
// diagnostic, exactly like `x.foo`. XFAIL: the implementation instead lexes
// `1.` greedily as a trailing-dot float, so `1.foo` errors as `expected ; or
// }` (ASI after the float) rather than as a selector. Divergence -- decide
// spec vs impl: explorations/spec-todo.md (float-digit-dot-selector, §5.8).
func main() {
    var y int = 1.foo
    _ = y
}
